# Inventory Management System (Core Three)

## Overview
This project is an **Inventory Management System** built using **ASP.NET Core Razor Pages**, **Entity Framework Core**, and **SQL Server**.  
It allows a shop owner to manage products, track price history, monitor price alerts, and export data to CSV or PDF.  
The system now includes filtering, authentication, rate limiting, and anti-forgery protection for secure API use.

---

## Features Implemented

### 🧩 Core Features (Sprint 5)
- Add, edit, view, and delete products.
- Each product includes: **Name**, **Owner**, **Price**, and optional **Model** / **Category**.
- **Search** and **filter** products by text, category, or model.
- Track **price changes** through a dedicated `PriceHistory` table.
- **Pagination** and **sorting** by ID, price, category, date, etc.
- Unit and integration tests for key features.

### 📦 Secondary Features (Sprint 7)
- **Export products or history** to **CSV** and **PDF** using QuestPDF.
- **Price alerts** automatically generated when price changes exceed a set threshold.
- **Advanced filtering** (by price range, category, or created date).
- Dedicated **details** and **history** pages for each product.
- Integration of a **PriceChangeService** to handle alerts automatically.

### 🔒 Security & API Hardening (Sprint 8)
- **Global CSRF protection** on API write actions.
- **Rate limiting** for API endpoints (30 requests/minute).
- **HTTPS redirection** and **HSTS** enabled in production.
- **ASP.NET Identity** with roles (`Admin`, `Owner`).
- **Improved password policy** (min 8 chars, digits required, lockout after failed attempts).
- API group secured with **authorization** and **antiforgery validation**.
- **Swagger** enabled in development for testing API endpoints.

### ⚙️ DevOps Pipeline (Sprint 8)
- **GitHub Actions** workflow runs:
  - Build & test for .NET 8
  - CodeQL static analysis for security
- Continuous Integration pipeline executes on every push/PR.
- [![.NET Build & Test + CodeQL](https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>/actions/workflows/dotnet-ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/<your-username>/<your-repo>/actions/workflows/dotnet-ci.yml)

